From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jxlarrea <jx@jxl.me>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 07:58:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ARM64: configs: biscuit: Enable SLUB_DEBUG for slab
 statistics

Unreclaimable slab is about 40 MB on the Echo Dot (2nd gen), well above
CM14 on 3.18. Without SLUB_DEBUG, /sys/kernel/slab reports no object
counts, so there is no way to tell which caches hold it. Debugging stays
off unless slub_debug is on the command line.

Drop this once the slab is understood.
---
 arch/arm64/configs/biscuit_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/biscuit_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/biscuit_defconfig
index 46a91420..94786b53 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/biscuit_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/biscuit_defconfig
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@ CONFIG_CPUSETS=y
 CONFIG_MEMCG=y
 CONFIG_MEMCG_SWAP=y
 CONFIG_SYSCTL_SYSCALL=y
-# CONFIG_SLUB_DEBUG is not set
+CONFIG_SLUB_DEBUG=y
 CONFIG_CC_STACKPROTECTOR_STRONG=y
 CONFIG_MODULE_FORCE_LOAD=y
 CONFIG_MODULE_FORCE_UNLOAD=y
